id: ops-backend-capability
title: Report verified backend SDK capabilities without tracker writes
description: "Build a read-only assurance matrix for every explicitly configured directory, database and MCP adapter. Verify backend operation contracts separately from core command/schema discovery and package ecosystem readiness."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T20:04:57.459Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T12:00:03.334Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Synthetic directory/database/MCP adapters produce distinct supported, unsupported, unavailable and invariant_failed statuses; diagnostics never mutate the tracker or require Git; typed SDK and CLI with compact TOON/JSON and typed remedies; README and example; read-only public fleet copy validated outside Git; targeted tests, typecheck and lint locally plus npm and Bun release gates in CI."
risk: low
confidence: high
comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T20:05:34.420Z",codex-agent,"Overlap check: current core SDK exports command/schema capability discovery and complete-list certification, but no configured backend contract assurance matrix. Sibling pm-web doctor checks database reachability/schema and its capability route discovers commands; pm-context/pm-observer do not verify backend read operations. Cargo readiness remains separate in ops-d8k3. No duplicate backend item found. PR 188 reconciliation items are excluded. Design: fixed read-only list/get/schema contracts, typed per-operation statuses and remedies, directory snapshot isolation to contain SDK-derived caches, and explicit read-port bridges for database/MCP providers. No write operations are probed."
  "2026-10-21T20:12:56.552Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replaced only auditBackendCapabilities with an empty success report, keeping all other functions unchanged. node --test --test-name-pattern \"matrix distinguishes\" test/backend-capabilities.test.ts failed 1/1 (exit 1) on missing operation statuses. Restored source immediately. Targeted backend plus renderer tests passed 16/16 before final hardening. Local build, test typecheck, lint and docstring gate passed; full npm/Bun gates remain delegated to CI on the final PR head."
  "2026-10-21T20:14:18.409Z",codex-agent,"Real-data validation: exported the public pm-ops origin/main tracker (eba7d5262fd75e67afce0caad29dae7dc7dfbaeb) to a non-Git temporary directory, made its directories/files read-only, removed Git from PATH, and audited it through the configured adapter SDK. All 300 source files retained identical aggregate SHA-256 evidence. Measured: 146 list items, one deterministic get, 11 schema types; 3 supported, 0 unsupported/unavailable/invariant_failed/unverified. Validation exposed preserved read-only snapshot directory modes; fixed owned-snapshot cleanup and added a regression. No tracker content was modified."
  "2026-10-21T20:15:13.794Z",codex-agent,"Pinned CLI linked acceptance completed: node --test test/backend-capabilities.test.ts test/renderer-ownership.test.ts passed 17/17, no skips or failures. pm test --run --progress passed its 1/1 linked command. Tracker test-result tracking is disabled by existing policy, so the verified counts are retained in this comment without changing policy. npm run build, npm run build:test, npm run lint, npm run docstring and npm run duplication passed (259 documented declarations; 0 clone pairs)."
  "2026-10-21T20:17:21.973Z",codex-agent,"Final focused c8 run: 10 backend tests passed with statements/branches/functions/lines all 100%. Packed npm archive installed into a real non-Git scratch tracker; actual pm ops capabilities returned clean TOON and JSON, exit 0, 3 supported operations (1 list item, 1 get, 11 types), with Git absent from PATH and byte-identical tracker files after both invocations. Pinned CLI local-directory install hit its 10000-entry scan ceiling; its documented npm-pack remedy succeeded. Local strict health is blocked by an inherited global pm-github extension requiring CLI 2026.10.21 while this repo pins 2026.10.17; no pin or global configuration changed. Fresh CI remains the health/release authority."
  "2026-10-21T21:44:05.348Z",codex-agent,"PR 189 review round: one unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M6u9WmW is valid: default capability audit must use the host-resolved pm_root. Latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff or nitpick findings. Branch includes current main. Plan: distinguish resolved root from cwd and global path, prove the regression fails with only handler behavior reverted, review the full PR for related routing defects, run targeted tests plus typecheck/lint, and use npm/Bun CI release gates as full-gate evidence."
  "2026-10-21T21:47:51.722Z",codex-agent,"Verified PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M6u9WmW: ops capabilities now binds its default directory adapter to CommandHandlerContext.pm_root. Added a real plain-directory tracker regression covering omitted and conflicting global path options while cwd points elsewhere; source bytes remain unchanged. Removed the old harness calls that omitted the required host context, and documented host-resolved selection. Full PR self-review found no other instance of this tracker-routing defect; explicit config roots remain relative to their config file. Behavioral revert proof: restored only the handler root expression to ctx.global.path with the prior default, leaving every other function and the test fixed. node --test --test-name-pattern \"default command audits the host-resolved tracker\" test/backend-capabilities.test.ts failed 1/1, exit 1, because it listed the cwd tracker instead of the selected tracker. Restored the fix immediately. node --test test/backend-capabilities.test.ts test/renderer-ownership.test.ts passed 18/18, zero failed/skipped. Restored regression passed through pm test --run --only-last --progress (1/1 linked command). npm run build, npm run build:test, npm run typecheck and npm run lint passed; committed dist rebuilt. No timeout retries needed. Existing test-result tracking policy is disabled, so results are retained here. Unchanged-threshold npm/Bun full release gates are delegated to exact-head CI; final run URLs and counts will be recorded in the PR description."
  "2026-10-22T11:15:10.164Z",codex-agent,"PR 189 review round: fetched every thread and all comments; the only unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M6vAUc4 is valid. Latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. Pulled the branch and merged current main 5804578; rebuilding the generated source map resolves its sole merge conflict. Cleanup now restores directory permissions before enumerating children, tolerates permission repair failure and always attempts removal without replacing audit evidence. Add filesystem fault regressions, prove behavioral revert failure, self-review the whole diff, then run unchanged npm and Bun release gates with isolated Git identity."
  "2026-10-22T11:21:11.262Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof for PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M6vAUc4: reverted only auditConfiguredBackends to the prior implementation, leaving the helper and regression fixed. node --test --test-name-pattern \"snapshot cleanup always\" test/backend-capabilities.test.ts failed 1/1, exit 1, because the injected directory enumeration error escaped before removal. Restored the implementation immediately. The regression scopes filesystem faults to the owned snapshot and verifies actual injection, removal and preserved three-operation audit evidence for enumeration, permission and removal failures. Self-review also corrected traversal order: restore each directory before listing its children, so mode-zero descendants can be removed. README documents best-effort cleanup. Isolated strict health passes; normal-home strict health sees an unrelated global pm-github host-version mismatch. No history rewrites or dependency pin changes."
  "2026-10-22T11:58:16.784Z",codex-agent,"Local npm release gate: 1399 tests total, 1396 passed, 2 existing optional real-data skips, 1 installed-routing package-install ETIMEDOUT at its unchanged 120-second subprocess limit under heavy host load. All measured coverage dimensions are 100%, including backend-capabilities.ts; lint, typecheck, zero-duplication and docstring gates passed. The new regression passed in the full suite and through the linked pm test (1/1). A focused installed-routing retry uses Node 26, isolated Git identity and the existing npm content cache. Full npm and Bun release gates will be verified in exact-head CI before starting PR 188; no thresholds or timeouts are changed."
  "2026-10-22T12:00:03.333Z",codex-agent,"Installed-routing retry passed 1/1 with no skips or failures: node --test --test-name-pattern \"installed pm CLI routes\" test/ops.test.ts on Node 26 with isolated HOME/Git identity and the existing npm cache. The unchanged test exercised packed runtime installation, deep doctor, no-pm fallback, explicit metrics JSON and fleet routing. This recovers the sole local full-suite timeout; no source, threshold or timeout change was needed. npm run audit:prod, npm run pack:dry-run, npm run changelog:check, npm run verify:release-changelog-date, npm run verify:release-publish-attestation and npm run verify:lifecycle-policy all passed. Full npm and Bun CI gates remain required before proceeding to PR 188. Item remains in_progress and claim released for orchestrator verification."
